Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Qore SSH server module packages
===============================

This is a development snapshot for the qore-testing PPA, not a final release.
The native module uses distribution libssh. Four user modules are delivered as
source and AOT code: SftpServerDataProvider, SshServerAuthProvider,
SshServerConnections and SshServerCommandProvider. Compiler metadata, provider
resources and translations accompany the runtime. API references, test fixtures
and examples are in qore-ssh-module-doc; debug symbols are generated separately.
Examples retain sibling test/ and demos/ directories so public key fixtures resolve.
Installing this package starts no service and creates no keys or accounts.

Build natively with dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc using the packaged Qore 3 SDK.
The build requires no network access and supports nocheck, nodoc, arch-only and
indep-only builds. Fixed qcc partitions and preserved AOT metadata make output
reproducible and usable by fresh compiler processes. Cross builds are rejected
because host qore/qpp tools are required. No prebuilt upstream artifacts ship.

Tests require OpenSSH client binaries and use ephemeral loopback SSH servers.
No external account, server or private credential is needed. Sandbox fixtures
explicitly allow 127.0.0.1/32, including the cancellation test; the denial
fixture proves that a denied range overrides that allow-list. The committed
keys in test/data are PUBLIC TEST IDENTITIES; never use them for deployment.
The full build runs all test/*.qtest, examples/*.qtest and examples/*.qr with
assertions enabled, plus strict provider translation checks. Installed autopkgtests repeat runtime
suites away from the checkout and compile a fresh program against the SDK.
Scaffold.qtest checks repository source/design files and runs only in the source
build, not the installed runtime test. Tests may use temporary files and sockets.
The old-libssh key-format fallback can skip format tests; qualification must
record skips explicitly. Ubuntu 26.04 qualification uses libssh with full support.

Before general publication, qualify target Debian/Ubuntu releases and
architectures, freeze Qore ABI and dependency versions, test relevant upgrades,
and sign/upload sources after review. A successful local build is not proof
that Launchpad has published the packages. Independent modules must be built
against the same qualified SDK and its runtime dependencies.
